  VALUES
    ('ios_crash_gate', 'iOS crash gate', 'blocked', 'Authenticated App Store Connect confirms one iOS 1.0.1 crash on 2026-08-25, but privacy suppression exposes no device, OS, crash report, stack, or UUID. Predecessor product commit 9c2dce4200dbba5487c8c458ade4616005fde6e6 retains preventive storage-failure hardening and passing regression suites. Historical hosted run 33296238901 for predecessor authority fb591e3d16f507a5a4f794ae537ccd087523889b passed its ordinary unsigned iOS job, including shared iOS Simulator tests, Apple glanceable-surface tests, and the unsigned application build. Those results cannot identify or be attributed to the historical event and do not transfer to current source authority 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6. Diagnostic access and symbolication, an exact signed physical iPhone/iPad pass, and post-rollout crash evidence remain missing.', 'Obtain any diagnostic report Apple later exposes, symbolicate if available, run exact signed physical iPhone QA, and collect post-rollout evidence'),
    ('open_meteo_promotion_clearance', 'Open-Meteo promotion clearance', 'pass', 'The complete authenticated Gmail record was checked read-only on 2026-08-29. The 06:05:07 +05:00 request described Nimbo as free and non-monetized, with no subscriptions, advertising, paid features, affiliate links, accounts, analytics SDK, or sale of user data, and limited promotion to unpaid localized posts, one personalized contact plus at most one follow-up, genuine Apple/Google editorial submissions, and ordinary unpaid links. At 17:25 +05:00, Nicoletta Addimando via OpenMeteo GmbH replied in ticket 234272 and explicitly confirmed that under those terms Nimbo is entitled to use the non-commercial API. This pass is limited to that exact scope and the published Free API limits; monetization, paid promotion, attribution removal, limit changes, or other material facts require a new licensing decision.', 'Preserve the confirmed scope and reopen licensing review before any material monetization, promotion, attribution, endpoint, or usage-limit change'),
    ('release_artifact_source_sync', 'Release artifact source sync', 'blocked', 'Product/build-input commit 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6 resolves to Android phone 1.1.0 (8), Wear OS 1.1.0 (1000008), and Apple 1.1.0 (6). It inherits the deterministic Compose UI harness, API 24 core-library desugaring, standard GitHub-hosted API 24/API 36 phone/tablet matrix, fail-closed KVM/hardware-acceleration gate, fail-closed NimboSourceRevision plumbing, deterministic bundle-specific App Store profiles, the non-upload export map, and strict verification metadata with 1,758 artifact entries. It replaces the generic Android UI-test activity with a dedicated activity that applies the requested locale to its base configuration before composition, verifies that Compose resources observe the injected language, and derives layout direction from the same locale while retaining all five tests and their exact Uzbek, Arabic, Russian, RTL, 200% text, accessibility, onboarding, success, cache, and recovery assertions. Historical hosted run 33296238901 at evidence commit 23617f361671a35245b2a892631fab73025b09b0 belongs to predecessor authority fb591e3d16f507a5a4f794ae537ccd087523889b: ordinary Android and the ordinary unsigned iOS job passed; the KVM gate passed on all three UI jobs; each UI job launched five tests and failed the same two zero-node Uzbek/Russian selectors because the generic activity reset locale, so the run failed overall. That run is historical and non-transferable; targeted local device-test ktlint, compilation, and manifest processing passed for 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6, but no hosted rerun exists for it. The branch-restricted release-signing environment exists but has 0/8 required secrets, the manual candidate workflow has not run, and the local login Keychain still rejects protected Android credential reads and Apple private-key use. The schema-v2 manifest keeps all three current artifact hashes and signing/physical evidence null; 0/3 artifacts are byte-verified and the gate remains blocked.', 'Run the standard hosted Android/iOS jobs and API 24/API 36 phone/tablet UI matrix for the current source, then unlock the local login Keychain, provision the protected release-signing environment, run the master-only hosted workflow, promote its verified receipt, and bind exact physical QA to the retained bytes'),
    ('android_physical_smoke', 'Android device smoke', 'blocked', 'Predecessor product commit 9c2dce4200dbba5487c8c458ade4616005fde6e6 retains physical API 25 phone and API 24/API 36 emulator regression evidence, including search without location, live forecast, cached offline fallback, retry recovery, widget rendering, and process-health checks. Those debug results are non-transferable and do not prove current upload-signed bytes. Historical hosted run 33296238901 for predecessor authority fb591e3d16f507a5a4f794ae537ccd087523889b passed the KVM gate on all three Android UI jobs; each job launched exactly five tests and each failed the same two localized Uzbek/Russian title selectors because the generic test activity reapplied device configuration and Compose resources remained on the system locale. Current authority 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6 uses a dedicated test activity that applies the requested locale before composition, verifies that Compose observes the injected language, and derives layout direction from the same locale. Targeted Android device-test ktlint, compilation, and merged-manifest processing passed locally, but no hosted rerun or signed artifact exists yet. There is no source-current upload-signed phone rerun, physical tablet/widget result, or paired physical Wear OS result. The gate remains blocked.', 'Sign and verify phone vc8, then run the exact signed artifact on phone and tablet plus widget and paired Wear OS paths'),
    ('ios_physical_smoke', 'iOS physical smoke', 'blocked', 'Predecessor product commit 9c2dce4200dbba5487c8c458ade4616005fde6e6 retains simulator-only Apple 1.1.0 (6) app/widget/watch builds with UUID-matched dSYMs, passing shared and Swift surface suites, and twelve bounded EN/RU/UZ phone creative sources. Historical hosted run 33296238901 for predecessor authority fb591e3d16f507a5a4f794ae537ccd087523889b passed its ordinary unsigned iOS job in 20m38s, including shared iOS Simulator tests, Apple glanceable-surface tests, and the unsigned application build. The overall run still failed on all three Android UI jobs, and none of that evidence transfers to current source authority 704fd893e59d94d8e9a4971313a773b3fa545ab6. There is no source-current distribution-signed archive or IPA, iOS 15 runtime pass, or physical iPhone/iPad/widget/paired-watch result. Current CoreDevice readiness must be re-established after signing succeeds. The gate remains blocked.', 'Create and verify distribution-signed build 6, re-establish CoreDevice readiness, then run the exact artifact on iPhone, iPad, widget, and paired watch paths'),
    ('domain_activation', 'Domain activation', 'pass', 'At 2026-08-29 10:40–10:41 +05:00, authenticated GitHub Pages settings showed DNS check successful and Enforce HTTPS enabled. The Let''s Encrypt certificate has CN nimbo.uz, SANs nimbo.uz/www.nimbo.uz, and validates for both hosts. WHOIS, .uz delegation, authoritative Cloudflare records, and independent 1.1.1.1/8.8.8.8 resolution pass. HTTPS returns 200 with verification result 0 for all 12 published UZ-root/RU/EN landing, press, privacy, and support routes plus growth, robots, sitemap, and the valid metadata schema. HTTP apex redirects to HTTPS; HTTP www reaches HTTPS apex in two redirects; HTTPS www redirects directly to HTTPS apex. All 12 localized HTML routes have the expected HTTPS canonical and language. Uzbek intentionally uses ' || chr(47) || ' rather than a separate ' || chr(47) || 'uz' || chr(47) || ' route.', 'Maintain dated DNS, certificate, redirect, canonical, and localized-route verification at each release'),
    ('store_policy_console_clearance', 'Store policy console clearance', 'pass', 'The 2026-08-28 App Store read-only check found no open review/compliance action. Google Play reported no policy issues at 2026-08-29 13:12 +05:00; production remained active at 1.0.2 (6), 100%. At 13:59:40 +05:00, UZ Custom Store Listing 4834799756935529888 was saved only as Draft, not submitted for review or published; Publishing overview still showed the latest publication on 2026-08-27. This is point-in-time Console evidence, not a guarantee against later review. See growth/quality/store-policy-console-2026-08-28.md and growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-29.md.', 'Re-check both app-global store policy surfaces at the next evidence cutoff')
